.TH MAINUAN-FLATPAK-INSTALL-GUI 1 "October 2026" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mainuan-flatpak-install-gui \- Mainuan Instalador Flatpak
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mainuan-flatpak-install-gui
.RB [ --scope " user|system|system:ID" ]
.RB [ --override-appname " name" ]
.RI [ file.flatpakref ]
.br
.B mainuan-flatpak-install-gui --remove --scope
.I user|system|system:ID file.flatpakref
.br
.B mainuan-flatpak-install-gui --demo
.RI [ state ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Version 1.0. Opens a Qt 6 and Kirigami window for a local Flatpak
reference. With no file, offers a graphical file selector. User installation is
selected initially. Install authorizes the app and required signed repositories;
origin information is in collapsed details. Real ambiguity requires a choice.
Installed apps offer Open and Uninstall for the exact selected copy. Uninstall
asks for confirmation and preserves personal data, repositories and runtimes.
.PP
Run as a normal desktop user. Flatpak and the session Polkit agent handle
required authorization according to effective policy. A password is not required
for every system operation. Cancellation does not undo completed changes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --scope user|system|system:ID
Select a user, default system or named system installation. Required for removal.
.TP
.B --remove
Remove the exact application reference from the local file and selected scope,
with graphical confirmation. Bare application IDs are not accepted.
.TP
.B --override-appname NAME
Use plain text NAME for presentation only; never changes operation identity.
.TP
.BR --demo " [ready|remote|progress|success|error|cancelled]"
Show an isolated demonstration without a real backend. Cannot be combined with
file, scope, removal or name override.
.TP
.B --help
Show command usage.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
flatpak-install-gui enters this same Qt application. The supported input is a local .flatpakref file. Bare IDs and URLs are outside
the product scope and are rejected with a clear error.
The internal Bash flags --fetch-dependencies and --do-install are retired and
exit with a clear error without performing operations.
.SH MIME
The desktop ID is mainuan-flatpak-install-gui.desktop. MIME support alone does
not select the default application. As the desktop user, run:
.PP
.nf
xdg-mime default mainuan-flatpak-install-gui.desktop application/vnd.flatpak.ref
xdg-mime query default application/vnd.flatpak.ref
.fi
.PP
A distribution integration fragment is installed under
/usr/share/mainuan-flatpak-install-gui/mainuan-mimeapps.list.
Personal MIME preferences take precedence over distribution defaults.
